1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,774
The first promise was made at the graduation ceremony, in the cold of a western winter: each graduate would publish one chapter of the group's history.

2
00:00:09,774 --> 00:00:19,797
“The goal is not the size of the report,” the director said at the meeting, “it is the duty to hand over the primary record.”

3
00:00:19,797 --> 00:00:27,121
The average reader of the index would never see the distribution of the evidence, and that was the point.

4
00:00:27,121 --> 00:00:31,635
“A dead archive is a kind of lie,” Maya said.

5
00:00:31,635 --> 00:00:44,008
“A present-tense account is a kind of evidence.” The spirit of the assignment was to write down the origin of every number, including the ones with a fault.

6
00:00:44,008 --> 00:00:47,942
The moment of conversion came with a photograph.

7
00:00:47,942 --> 00:00:53,516
“This image is identical to the one in the party's leaflet,” Lin said.

8
00:00:53,516 --> 00:01:04,929
“We have tied our history to a political leaflet, and we did not notice.” The stake was not money but the taste of the whole project.

9
00:01:04,929 --> 00:01:12,667
The rough draft of the fifth chapter had a tie to an antique map and a reserve of unprocessed field notes.

10
00:01:12,667 --> 00:01:18,736
“A trick of presentation will not save a weak index,” the director said.

11
00:01:18,736 --> 00:01:25,890
“A sacrifice is required, and it is the sacrifice of the pretty sentence.”

12
00:01:25,890 --> 00:01:29,645
The confusion in the room was about ownership.

13
00:01:29,645 --> 00:01:36,064
“Only ten of us wrote it, and even the town has a claim,” the editor said.

14
00:01:36,064 --> 00:01:48,182
“We cannot cling to a private sphere and call it public scholarship.” The reward for publishing was, in the end, the release itself.

15
00:01:48,182 --> 00:02:04,008
A faint frost on the window, a stroke of the pen, and the preview of the last page: the promise was convert into a series of small assignments, and the convertible one was the only one the group could honestly sign.

16
00:02:04,008 --> 00:02:09,442
The ten of us met then, and the section on the party was the hardest.

17
00:02:09,442 --> 00:02:19,230
A type of town, a certain world, a town that would not die: the evidence was political even when we said that it was not.

18
00:02:19,230 --> 00:02:27,144
We had to show the break in the record and let the reader see it, and only the town could decide what to publish.

19
00:02:27,144 --> 00:02:33,122
The present page would seem to choke on its own inclination.
